WEBVTT

00:16.610 --> 00:19.510
Taiyou ni me ga kurameba

00:19.510 --> 00:24.190
hikari no hate o shiru darou

00:24.190 --> 00:26.090
Hoshikuzu no nou

00:26.090 --> 00:31.930
Nante semai uchuu de boku wa ikiteru

00:31.930 --> 00:39.470
Dare ka zero kara hajimeru
koodo o sazukete kurenai ka

00:39.470 --> 00:42.040
Zoushoku sare sakuran

00:42.040 --> 00:46.070
Hako no naka shiseru koronii

00:46.070 --> 00:50.550
Kakan naki yume o ute

00:50.550 --> 00:53.720
Kodoku yo jibaku seyo

00:53.720 --> 00:58.120
Yubisaki no mirai ni

00:58.120 --> 01:01.960
donna sakurifaisu ga arou to

01:01.960 --> 01:05.630
Mune no oku de

01:05.630 --> 01:08.930
Kokoro koushin seyo

01:08.930 --> 01:13.070
Ippo kako no hibi ga

01:13.070 --> 01:16.070
toozakatte yukedomo

01:16.070 --> 01:23.140
Koishikarubeki kimi

01:47.970 --> 01:50.940
There are two kinds of smugglers.

01:50.940 --> 01:52.940
Smugglers who deliver goods...

01:52.940 --> 01:55.430
and smugglers who deliver thoughts.

01:56.040 --> 01:58.850
As for myself, I'll carry either one...

01:58.850 --> 02:01.280
as long as the money's there.

02:03.890 --> 02:07.990
No matter how risky
the package turns out to be.

02:07.990 --> 02:12.950
"There are Two Kinds of Smugglers"

02:17.970 --> 02:20.640
How'd we ever get ourselves
into this situation, bear-o?!

02:20.640 --> 02:24.540
It's all because of Morte trying
to eat that can of sand whale!

02:24.540 --> 02:26.800
Stop blaming other people!

02:40.360 --> 02:42.720
What the... Those guys again?!

02:42.720 --> 02:45.990
This makes the second time I've found 'em
on the verge of drowning in the Sand Sea.

02:45.990 --> 02:48.550
I guess those clowns never learn.

03:01.040 --> 03:04.750
So you guys're heading for
the autumn continent too, eh?

03:04.750 --> 03:08.950
Lucky for you, I was just on
my way there to make a delivery.

03:08.950 --> 03:12.120
So if you want, I can take
the three of you along with me.

03:12.120 --> 03:14.590
I'll just tell you right now...
we don't have any money, bear-o.

03:14.590 --> 03:16.960
In that case, you can work for your passage...

03:16.960 --> 03:19.860
swabbing the decks and keeping the cabins clean.

03:19.860 --> 03:23.230
And now that I think of it, the
kitchen's getting pretty disgusting, too.

03:23.230 --> 03:24.100
What do you say?

03:24.100 --> 03:27.270
If this ship is spic 'n' span by the
time we reach the autumn continent,

03:27.270 --> 03:28.570
I won't charge you a thing.

03:28.570 --> 03:32.140
Really? In that case,
you've got yourself a deal!

03:32.140 --> 03:35.580
Hey! Who made you the decider for all of us?!

03:47.490 --> 03:50.090
Not those guys from the World
Salvation Committee again, bear-o?!

03:50.090 --> 03:52.890
Stop standing there
like an idiot and return fire!

03:52.890 --> 03:56.100
Hey, this is just a carrier
vessel, not some battleship.

03:56.100 --> 03:59.430
Sorry to disappoint you, but we don't have
any weapons we can use against torpedoes.

04:03.970 --> 04:06.310
Listen here, you filthy smuggler scum!

04:06.310 --> 04:08.310
Time to give it up!

04:08.310 --> 04:12.080
We'll be takin' that cargo off your
hands now, so don't go givin' us no trouble!

04:12.980 --> 04:16.680
It doesn't seem like they're
after us this time, bear-o!

04:20.860 --> 04:22.160
That symbol...

04:22.160 --> 04:24.150
It's the mark of the Golden Lions!

04:28.200 --> 04:31.300
All right, hand the cargo over to us now!

04:31.300 --> 04:34.840
Or else we're gonna ram another torpedo right
through yer ship's belly and split 'er wide...

04:34.840 --> 04:36.870
Huh?

04:36.870 --> 04:38.440
Those three?!

04:38.440 --> 04:41.680
It's the World Destruction Committee!

04:41.680 --> 04:42.880
Well, I'll be!

04:42.880 --> 04:46.140
Talk about killin' two birds with one stone!

04:56.160 --> 05:00.230
It seems the World Destruction
Committee's been taken captive by a subarenine.

05:00.230 --> 05:03.330
They just happened to be on
board some unlucky smuggler's ship.

05:03.330 --> 05:06.800
And I'll bet they were heading for
the autumn continent, weren't they?

05:06.800 --> 05:10.740
I just think it's a terrible shame that we
couldn't have been the ones to capture them.

05:10.740 --> 05:14.140
Apparently the subarenine got
an anonymous tip from someone...

05:14.140 --> 05:17.550
that the Golden Lions were trying to
smuggle some goods onto the autumn continent...

05:17.550 --> 05:21.180
and they were on a mission to seize those goods.

05:21.180 --> 05:24.190
So... what's your point?

05:24.190 --> 05:27.560
I'm wondering who leaked the
information about the smuggled goods.

05:27.560 --> 05:30.060
If I'm right, then...

05:30.060 --> 05:31.560
I think it would behoove us

05:31.560 --> 05:35.720
to retrieve the Destruct Code from
the subarenine as soon as possible.

05:53.550 --> 05:56.280
Hey... so you know about the Golden Lions?

05:56.280 --> 05:59.590
They're a two-bit resistance group.

05:59.590 --> 06:03.930
"Two-bit," huh?
Well, you could be right about that.

06:03.930 --> 06:07.100
So tell us why you were
carrying cargo for them, bear-o.

06:07.100 --> 06:10.060
Are you a member of the
resistance yourself, bear-o?

06:10.060 --> 06:12.470
Me? Nah, I've got nothing to do with them.

06:12.470 --> 06:16.560
I already told you... I'll carry
anything as long as the money's there.

06:18.270 --> 06:19.440
And what's more,

06:19.440 --> 06:22.780
once I take on a job, I see it
through to the end no matter what.

06:22.780 --> 06:24.910
That's my creed.

06:24.910 --> 06:28.750
And so far there hasn't been a single
package I haven't been able to deliver.

06:28.750 --> 06:31.550
So you're saying you've
got some kind of plan, bear-o?

06:31.550 --> 06:32.650
Somebody help me!

06:32.650 --> 06:34.160
- What's all that racket?!
- Someone get in here!

06:34.160 --> 06:37.230
- You three're gettin' on my nerves!
- Stop her! Stop her! Stop her!

06:37.230 --> 06:39.750
You're the one who's getting on our nerves!

06:45.330 --> 06:49.240
There's an emergency! The World
Destruction Committee prisoners have escaped!

06:49.240 --> 06:52.570
We're on the surface of the Sand Sea...
there's nowhere they can escape to!

06:52.570 --> 06:56.010
Captain! We have a sand ship
approaching from the bow!

06:56.010 --> 06:56.940
What?!

06:58.780 --> 07:01.450
They think they can snatch the
glory right out from under me?!

07:01.450 --> 07:02.480
Well I ain't handin' 'em over!

07:02.480 --> 07:04.180
Dive!

07:07.860 --> 07:09.020
Those fools...

07:09.020 --> 07:10.620
Let's go, Lia!

07:17.600 --> 07:20.860
This is bad! They're taking us under!

07:41.190 --> 07:44.160
I wouldn't go near those boxes if I were you.

07:45.330 --> 07:50.230
Did any of you know what was in
those boxes when you took the job?

07:50.230 --> 07:52.060
What are you talking about?

07:54.500 --> 07:55.670
I'm just a smuggler...

07:55.670 --> 07:59.310
it doesn't make any difference to
me what's inside. I carry anything.

07:59.310 --> 08:04.300
Those guns are just a cover.
Here's the real cargo...

08:11.590 --> 08:12.890
Is that a?

08:12.890 --> 08:15.080
A time bomb, bear-o?!

08:17.690 --> 08:20.230
Just the kind of thing I'd
expect from the Golden Lions.

08:20.230 --> 08:21.860
What do you mean by that?

08:21.860 --> 08:26.170
The whole thing was the
Golden Lions' plan right from the start.

08:26.170 --> 08:29.400
Get some clueless, pea-brained
smuggler to carry a load of cargo...

08:29.400 --> 08:33.210
leak the news to the beastmen and
trick them into confiscating the cargo...

08:33.210 --> 08:34.440
and ba-boom.

08:34.440 --> 08:37.040
I think "pea-brained"
was a little uncalled for...

08:37.040 --> 08:39.050
Those guys have no morals!

08:39.050 --> 08:42.180
Okay, but... shouldn't we be chucking
that thing outside right about now?!

08:42.180 --> 08:44.720
We have to get them to
surface the ship right away, bear-o!

08:44.720 --> 08:46.450
That ain't gonna happen!

08:46.450 --> 08:48.360
I ain't fallin' for yer lies!

08:48.360 --> 08:50.760
I captured these prisoners...

08:50.760 --> 08:52.630
and I'm gonna get the credit for it!

08:52.630 --> 08:56.960
You can try and fool me all
you want, but it ain't gonna fly.

08:56.960 --> 08:58.530
You're even stupider than I thought.

08:58.530 --> 09:01.240
You all! What're you
doin' standin' there like that?!

09:01.240 --> 09:03.970
Hurry up and secure these
World Destruction Committee hooligans!

09:03.970 --> 09:05.400
Yessir!

09:06.910 --> 09:08.640
What should we do?

09:08.640 --> 09:09.910
Nothing we can do.

09:09.910 --> 09:12.970
But in the meantime
let's deactivate that trigger.

09:23.930 --> 09:24.730
That's not good!

09:24.730 --> 09:26.230
It's gonna blow!

09:26.230 --> 09:28.420
Run, bear-o!

09:37.570 --> 09:40.600
Lia, what are you doing?! Hurry!

09:47.010 --> 09:49.280
You bastards! Open this door!

09:49.280 --> 09:51.420
Open up!

09:51.420 --> 09:53.440
W-Wait for me!

10:20.110 --> 10:21.450
Kyrie!

10:39.200 --> 10:41.700
It's not working!
We've gotta get this thing off him!

10:41.700 --> 10:43.330
We have to hurry!

10:58.490 --> 11:00.420
He's not breathing...

11:00.420 --> 11:02.250
He needs mouth-to-mouth!

11:03.260 --> 11:05.830
Wha... I can't! I don't even know how!

11:05.830 --> 11:07.700
Why don't you do it?!

11:07.700 --> 11:11.600
Well I don't know how to, either.

11:11.600 --> 11:13.670
Wh-What are you looking at me for?!

11:13.670 --> 11:16.670
It's not like I owe him my life or... anything.

11:16.670 --> 11:18.340
I'll do it, bear-o!

11:18.340 --> 11:19.740
Toppy!

11:19.740 --> 11:23.340
Kyrie, I'm gonna save you now, bear-o.

11:32.750 --> 11:34.390
T-T-T-T-T-T-T-T-T-T-T-T-Toppy!

11:34.390 --> 11:36.360
Wh-What're you d-d-doing?!

11:36.360 --> 11:38.290
Wha... hey, don't go
getting the wrong idea, bear-o!

11:38.290 --> 11:40.350
It's called mouth-to-mouth resuscitation!

11:45.870 --> 11:46.800
Kyrie!

11:46.800 --> 11:47.700
Lia!

11:47.700 --> 11:48.930
This way, bear-o!

11:51.810 --> 11:54.140
We've gotta get out of here, too! Let's go!

12:02.150 --> 12:04.880
We should be fine inside here for a while.

12:09.920 --> 12:12.730
What happened to Kyrie and the others?

12:12.730 --> 12:15.630
They managed to get away through
one of the doorways, just like us.

12:15.630 --> 12:18.060
I think they should be fine.

12:18.670 --> 12:19.830
So we're here...

12:19.830 --> 12:21.600
Where's that?

12:21.600 --> 12:23.300
This room is...

12:33.850 --> 12:36.020
Lia, are you all right?

12:36.020 --> 12:38.420
Nadja? I'm just fine.

12:38.420 --> 12:40.820
So's the man from the World
Destruction Committee... and, uh...

12:42.360 --> 12:43.760
so's the... bear.

12:43.760 --> 12:45.590
Don't call me a bear, bear-o!

12:45.590 --> 12:47.030
That's good news!

12:47.030 --> 12:49.330
Everyone here is safe, too.

13:03.810 --> 13:07.310
I'd say that means we just
reached the bottom of the Sand Sea.

13:07.310 --> 13:09.820
Can't we surface?

13:09.820 --> 13:13.280
No way... the engines aren't responding.

13:14.560 --> 13:18.690
It looks like the shock from the
explosion took out our ability to surface.

13:18.690 --> 13:23.460
So what you're saying is... we're
trapped here at the bottom of the Sand Sea?

13:28.740 --> 13:29.870
If we stay down here,

13:29.870 --> 13:33.170
it's only a matter of time before the
sand pressure crushes the hull, bear-o!

13:33.170 --> 13:36.040
Aren't we gonna run out of air, too?

13:36.040 --> 13:37.910
Call for help right now!

13:37.910 --> 13:41.320
One more thing... you'd better keep quiet
about the fact that we're here with you!

13:41.320 --> 13:44.080
We have no means of communication.

13:44.080 --> 13:48.860
And even if we were able to contact someone,
no one could make it down here to save us.

13:48.860 --> 13:50.220
What do you mean?!

13:50.220 --> 13:55.330
The subarenine was only just recently
developed by an engineer in Clock Town.

13:55.330 --> 13:59.000
Which means that the vessel we're in...
is the only subarenine in existence.

13:59.000 --> 14:01.840
So then, why don't we just
swim our way out of here?

14:01.840 --> 14:04.570
Are you crazy?! There's no way we'd make it!

14:04.570 --> 14:06.570
We're at the bottom of the Sand Sea...

14:06.570 --> 14:09.080
if we step outside the sand
pressure'll turn us into pancakes.

14:09.080 --> 14:11.780
But there ought to be something we can do.

14:11.780 --> 14:14.350
So in the interest of all of
us making it out of this alive...

14:14.350 --> 14:17.750
what do you say we call a temporary truce?

14:18.450 --> 14:21.560
Isn't the vessel equipped with some
kind of emergency escape mechanism?

14:21.560 --> 14:23.420
There's nothing nearly that sophisticated.

14:23.420 --> 14:26.390
So what did they think they'd do
when something like this happened?!

14:26.390 --> 14:28.860
Isn't it obvious that they thought
nothing like this would happen?

14:29.260 --> 14:31.470
So how far is it to the top, anyway?

14:31.470 --> 14:34.240
Can't we just hold our breath a long
time and somehow make it up there?

14:34.240 --> 14:40.470
Or I know! Maybe Toppy could blow air into
our mouths the way he did for me just now!

14:40.470 --> 14:42.880
You think I'm some kind of oxygen tank, bear-o?!

14:42.880 --> 14:44.250
Wait, that's a good idea!

14:44.250 --> 14:47.750
We could take these toilet bowls and
put them upside down over our heads!

14:47.750 --> 14:51.490
That way the air stays trapped inside
and we can still breathe under the sand!

14:51.490 --> 14:52.620
Like he just said!

14:52.620 --> 14:56.280
If we go outside, we'll get
flattened by the sand pressure!

14:58.290 --> 15:01.260
I'm very sorry about that...

15:02.000 --> 15:05.100
The cargo hold where the explosion
occurred is in the lower part of the ship...

15:05.100 --> 15:07.000
and the engines are
located fore of that location,

15:07.000 --> 15:09.340
so there's a good chance they're still intact.

15:09.340 --> 15:13.240
Assuming the only problem is that
we lack engine control from the cockpit...

15:13.240 --> 15:15.510
if we can somehow pilot the
ship directly from the engine room,

15:15.510 --> 15:17.110
we may be able to get moving again.

15:17.110 --> 15:20.010
But how do we get to the engine room?

15:20.010 --> 15:22.920
All the corridors are
filled to the brim with sand.

15:22.920 --> 15:25.790
We could move through these
ducts right here... or maybe...

15:25.790 --> 15:30.420
Aren't those air intake ducts? They're way
too small for you or me to climb through...

15:33.590 --> 15:35.130
So this is how it is...

15:35.130 --> 15:36.530
I just swallow my Little Bear pride

15:36.530 --> 15:41.330
while they keep right on treating
me like a plain old bear, bear-o?!

15:41.940 --> 15:44.630
I wonder if Toppy's all right...

15:57.480 --> 16:00.820
If the ducts fill up with
sand too, then that's all she wrote.

16:00.820 --> 16:03.860
It'll be fine. I know that bear...
he'll get the job done for sure.

16:03.860 --> 16:05.560
Don't call me a bear, bear-o!

16:05.560 --> 16:07.060
Toppy!

16:07.060 --> 16:10.400
Looks like I made it safely
to the engine room, bear-o.

16:10.400 --> 16:15.040
All right, try starting the engine
by hand now, just like I explained it.

16:15.040 --> 16:16.970
I'm trying it now, bear-o.

16:21.710 --> 16:23.480
This isn't gonna work, bear-o!

16:23.480 --> 16:25.410
What's wrong, Toppy?

16:25.410 --> 16:27.720
The fuel tanks are screwed, bear-o!

16:27.720 --> 16:31.990
All the fuel's leaked out...
the tanks are completely empty, bear-o!

16:31.990 --> 16:34.420
It seems like we've run out of tricks.

16:34.420 --> 16:38.980
So I guess it's just a matter of time
before we all get crushed in this tin can.

16:41.100 --> 16:45.430
Well, if the World
Destruction Committee is wiped out...

16:45.430 --> 16:49.840
then so is the reason for the
existence of the World Salvation Committee.

16:49.840 --> 16:52.840
If this is it, then I guess there are worse
ways to go than being annihilated together.

16:52.840 --> 16:57.510
So the pea-brained smuggler's
just collateral damage, then?

16:57.510 --> 16:59.010
Come to think about it,

16:59.010 --> 17:05.190
there was a job about a year back
that I wasn't able to deliver on, either...

17:05.190 --> 17:10.260
Only it wasn't goods that time...
I was supposed to deliver a message.

17:10.260 --> 17:13.890
The client was a member of the Golden Lions...

17:13.890 --> 17:17.350
but I thought that kid was way too
young to be mixed up in the resistance.

17:20.400 --> 17:22.630
Now what was it?

17:30.480 --> 17:33.250
He said something to me...

17:33.250 --> 17:35.920
about wanting me to deliver
a message to his older sister,

17:35.920 --> 17:39.250
who was waiting for him
back in their hometown.

17:40.090 --> 17:42.890
It was like "I'm sorry
for making you worried..."

17:42.890 --> 17:46.090
"but I will come home safe..."

17:46.090 --> 17:48.560
"and I will change the world..."

17:48.560 --> 17:51.620
"so please just wait for me until then."

17:53.730 --> 17:56.270
But before I could ask him
who to give the message to,

17:56.270 --> 17:58.670
he got called away by
his friends and took off.

17:59.570 --> 18:02.440
He did say she was strong-willed...

18:02.440 --> 18:06.650
and hard to deal with in a lot of ways...

18:06.650 --> 18:11.420
but that... deep down she was a kind...

18:11.420 --> 18:15.860
and really gutsy big sister.

18:18.630 --> 18:19.960
What do you think you're doing?

18:19.960 --> 18:21.460
As long as you've got
that message to deliver,

18:21.460 --> 18:26.130
we can't just sit still and
let you die here, now can we?

18:30.200 --> 18:31.710
You're wasting your time.

18:31.710 --> 18:35.180
With the fuel tanks out of commission,
there's just nothing we can do.

18:35.180 --> 18:39.550
Even if the tanks are dry, if we use the
small amount of fuel left in the engines...

18:39.550 --> 18:41.780
then we should be able to move,
even if it's just a little bit.

18:41.780 --> 18:46.950
Even if we are able to move just a little bit,
we're at the very bottom of a deep sea of sand.

18:46.950 --> 18:52.150
And with our surfacing capability gone, we'll
never be able to reach the surface of the sand.

19:02.400 --> 19:05.540
Something really huge is
scraping against the hull of the ship!

19:05.540 --> 19:10.740
Didn't you just tell us there were
no other subarenines in existence?

19:10.740 --> 19:12.510
That's no subarenine!

19:12.510 --> 19:14.210
I know that call...

19:14.210 --> 19:16.080
It's a sand whale!

19:21.320 --> 19:22.390
Toppy!

19:22.390 --> 19:24.390
Start up the engines!

19:24.390 --> 19:26.260
They don't have to last all the way to the top!

19:26.260 --> 19:29.530
If we can just move a tiny bit
forward, that should be enough!

19:29.530 --> 19:30.930
Roger, bear-o!

19:40.510 --> 19:42.670
Here goes nothing!

20:14.980 --> 20:19.280
Sand whales respond to noise, and
they swallow their prey whole, sand and all!

20:19.280 --> 20:22.720
Then they blow all the excess sand out!

20:59.320 --> 21:01.360
The autumn continent...

21:01.360 --> 21:03.660
It's a miracle, bear-o!

21:03.660 --> 21:05.930
That was no miracle...

21:05.930 --> 21:08.330
It was inevitable.

21:24.650 --> 21:26.780
So then? What do you plan to do?

21:26.780 --> 21:28.220
You intend to capture us?

21:28.220 --> 21:30.550
Hush up, Morte!

21:30.550 --> 21:34.490
Not this time...
I believe we're still under a truce.

21:34.490 --> 21:35.620
Nadja!

21:35.620 --> 21:37.560
So long.

21:37.560 --> 21:41.690
If they can, I really wish they'd
extend this truce indefinitely, bear-o.

21:46.970 --> 21:50.840
Well then, I suppose I'd
best be on my way now, too.

21:58.850 --> 22:00.410
What is it?

22:00.410 --> 22:02.540
Nothing at all...

22:04.380 --> 22:08.380
Looks like I managed
to deliver on that job after all.

22:21.230 --> 22:24.740
Kirameku suna no umi

22:24.740 --> 22:27.870
Aoi chijou no hate

22:27.870 --> 22:33.950
Yuuyami ni ochita sora kara

22:33.950 --> 22:37.080
afuredasu kioku

22:37.080 --> 22:40.290
Gareki no you ni

22:40.290 --> 22:46.290
kasanete yuku darou

22:46.290 --> 22:49.530
Meguriau inochi

22:49.530 --> 22:52.600
Surechigau kimochi

22:52.600 --> 22:55.740
Tsumugiau kotoba

22:55.740 --> 22:58.870
Kizutsukeau mono

22:58.870 --> 23:10.980
Sore demo bokura ga aruiteku
michi wa asu e tsuzuiteru no

23:13.820 --> 23:17.660
Ima o against the world ikiru imi wa

23:17.660 --> 23:20.660
